1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,360
你好吗
How we doin'?

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:06,460
今天是全年压力最大的日子
It's the most stressful day of the year

3
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:07,400
是对克莱尔来说
for Claire --

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,280
今天是结婚周年纪念日
our anniversary.

5
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:11,840
她总是到最后关头才去选礼物
She tends to leave her gift shopping till the last minute,

6
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,440
弄得自己压力很大
and the pressure can really get to her.

7
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:14,940
我很好啊
I'm great.

8
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,620
-你是不是忘了今天是... -我没忘
- Oh, did you forget it's our -- - No.

9
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:21,940
周年纪念日快乐
Happy Anniversary.

10
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:24,560
你平静得很离奇
You're strangely calm.

11
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,500
这是传说中疯到极点后的返疯归真之域吗
Is this the legendary realm beyond madness.

12
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,340
你的礼物我已经买好了
I already got your gift.

13
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:29,980
我选得特别成功
And I nailed it.

14
00:00:30,058 --> 00:00:32,121
而且没有超过一百块钱的预算限制
I even stayed below the $100 limit.

15
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:32,740
你呢
You?

16
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,360
你会很满意的
Oh, you'll be quite pleased.

17
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:35,880
等我找到礼物后
...once I find something.

18
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:38,200
这次我等到最后一刻才去买礼物
This time I left my shopping till the last minute,

19
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:41,140
可能是为了给克莱尔一个竞争的希望
maybe just to give Claire a chance at our competition.

20
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,460
我太好胜了吗
Am I too competitive?

21
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:44,920
她确实常说
I mean, she does often say,

22
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,100
"菲尔 你每次都要先到终点[高潮]吗"
"Phil, do you always have to finish first?"

23
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:50,740
乔 我来抓你啦
Joe, I'm coming for you.

24
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:53,060
你们见到乔了吗
Hey, have you guys seen Joe?

25
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,180
大兄弟
Aw, man!

26
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,418
你这么轻易就找到我了
You found me so easy.

27
00:00:57,418 --> 00:00:59,174
但好玩就好啦
But that was for fun.

28
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:00,558
躲猫猫
Hide and seek?

29
00:01:00,558 --> 00:01:02,002
当我4岁小屁孩吗
What am I, 4?

30
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:05,259
我来是因为卢克有最新的丧尸电子游戏
I'm here because Luke has the new zombie video game

31
00:01:05,259 --> 00:01:07,366
我妈绝不会让我玩
that my mom would never let me play.

32
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,980
还有什么
So...what else?

33
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:10,260
还有什么能玩呢
What else?

34
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:12,201
对了 你不是买了新的游戏吗
Hey, didn't you get a new video game?

35
00:01:12,201 --> 00:01:13,780
糟了 糟了 糟了 糟了
Crap, crap, crap, crap, crap!

36
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:15,540
-你昨天看到她了吗 -没有 怎么了
- Did you see her yesterday? - No, why?

37
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:16,920
她发现自己睡过了一整天
That's what she says when she realizes

38
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,240
就会这样骂
she just slept through an entire day.

39
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:19,720
我老板周末外出了
So, my boss went away for the weekend,

40
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:21,518
我发现我把手机落在她家了
and I realized I left my phone at her house.

41
00:01:21,518 --> 00:01:22,460
有一扇狗狗门可以进去
There's a doggy door,

42
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:23,820
但那样我就得先找只狗
but then I would have to find a dog,

43
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:24,980
想办法训练它进屋里去
somehow learn how to train it

44
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:26,300
再找到我的手机
to go inside, and then find it.

45
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:27,529
-我不知道上哪儿去找... -亲爱的
- And I don't know where to get a -- - Honey...

46
00:01:28,907 --> 00:01:30,245
天啊 我这都没想到
Oh my God, duh.

47
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,420
乔 你不就有只狗吗
Joe, you have a dog.

48
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:34,140
走吧
Come on.

49
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:53,740
看到没 那时娱乐行业还是有格调的
Now see, this is when entertainment was classy.

50
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:55,640
老艺人身穿礼服
Max Feldman wore a tux,

51
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,180
观众抽着雪茄
the audience smoked cigars.

52
00:01:57,180 --> 00:02:00,440
他的表演放到今天看 仍然跟七零年代时一样好笑
And his act is as fresh today as it was in the '70s.

53
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:01,700
怎么 你是爱斯基摩人吗
What are you, an Eskimo?

54
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,400
你懂50种雪的不同称呼
You got 50 words for "snow,"

55
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,080
但却不懂"牙刷"怎么叫
but apparently none for "toothbrush."

56
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:10,200
我不懂你们为什么喜欢这男的
I don't understand why you guys like that man.

57
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:11,180
他就是个欺负人的恶霸
He's a bully.

58
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,000
这就是为什么
See, this is why

59
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,520
我们今晚才不带你去看他的表演
we're not bringing you to his show tonight.

60
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:14,660
你听不懂笑话的哏
You don't get the jokes,

61
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:16,120
总是问个不停
you ask questions the whole time...

62
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,440
那会毁了观看感受
It ruins the experience.

63
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:19,580
我听得懂好笑的笑话
I understand funny jokes.

64
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,340
这不是好笑 是恶毒
This is not funny. This is mean.

65
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:22,500
他刚刚对那男的说
He just told that guy

66
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,960
他看起来像穿着晚礼服的牛肉干
that he looked like a beef jerky wearing a tuxedo.

67
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:27,658
那个男的是罗纳德·里根 他爱死这笑话了
And that guy was Ronald Reagan and he loved it!

68
00:02:27,658 --> 00:02:29,700
我希望费尔德曼今晚也吐槽我
I hope Feldman zetzes me tonight.

69
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,800
-所以你才穿上这件丑爆的衣服吗 -不是
- Is that why you're wearing that shirt? - Huh? No.

70
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,840
我要出门去办些事
Anyways, I'm gonna go and run some errands.

71
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:36,120
如果豪尔赫在我回来之前就到了
If Jorge arrives before I'm back,

72
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,780
拜托你们不要用这些玩意烦他
please don't bore him with this stuff.

73
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:40,120
豪尔赫是个骚气美型的拉丁音乐人
Jorge was this steamy Latin musician

74
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,060
你妈跟他交往过
your mother used to date.

75
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:43,320
显然她觉得必须邀请他来家里
Apparently she feels she has to invite him here,

76
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,780
而不是边翻看高中年刊
instead of just thinking about him

77
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:46,680
配着第三杯威士忌
while she pages through a high-school yearbook

78
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,900
边想着他
on her third Scotch

79
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,374
像个正常人一样
like a normal person.

80
00:02:49,374 --> 00:02:50,960
杰 别吃醋
Jay, don't be jealous.

81
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,180
那都是20年前的事了
It was 20 years ago,

82
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,280
再说我们只交往了6个月而已
and I only dated him for six months.

83
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,760
我们的感情远不如我跟你之间的深刻
And we never had what you and I have.

84
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:57,840
这话听了还挺开心
Well, that's nice to hear.

85
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:58,900
我只是沉迷他的肉体而已
It was only physical.

86
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:01,220
曼尼
Manny...

87
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:04,040
你今天要学点新知识
you're gonna learn something today.

88
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,320
我每天都尽量学习新知识
I try to learn something every day.

89
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:07,297
那让我保持青春活力
It keeps me young,

90
00:03:07,297 --> 00:03:09,300
用芬兰语说就是"牛哦狸"
or nuori, as they say in Finnish.

91
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,221
假设你能不再说这种瞎话
Assuming you stop saying stuff like that,

92
00:03:11,221 --> 00:03:12,620
终有一天你会娶到老婆
one day you will be married,

93
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:14,780
然后前任就会出现
and eventually the ex will show up

94
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:15,760
东闻西闻想抢你老婆
sniffing around,

95
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,740
挺起他小鲜肉的胸膛
puffing out his pretty-boy chest,

96
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,720
那时你就要拿出你的兽王气概
which is your cue to go alpha.

97
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,120
妈妈看到你对她老朋友不礼貌
Don't you think Mom will get annoyed

98
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,820
你觉得她不会生气吗
when she sees you being rude to an old friend?

99
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:23,600
完全不会
Not at all.

100
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,780
内心深处 她想看到我
Deep down, she wants to see me vanquish

101
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:26,960
完虐其他追求者
all who came before.

102
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,480
这是最基本的动物界原理
It's basic animal stuff.

103
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:29,780
我懂
Oh, I get it.

104
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:32,040
前几天晚上 我女友凯伦的前男友出现后
My girlfriend Karen was pretty frisky the other night

105
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:33,840
我跟他来了一场巧克力梳芙厘烘烤大对决
after her ex showed up, and I bested him

106
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,701
在我打败她后 她心情也很好
in a chocolate-souffle bake-off.

107
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:36,920
我不说你也能猜到
I don't need to tell you

108
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,200
她那晚"吃掉"的巧克力色甜点
my souffle wasn't the only sweet brown dish

109
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:40,420
不止我的梳芙厘
she devoured that night.

110
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:41,180
因为...
Because...?

111
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,080
我还做了黑糖曲奇
I also made molasses cookies.

112
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,000
所以我才学会了要问第二个问题
I've learned to ask the second question.

113
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,720
我都不记得为什么事打架了
I don't even remember what the fight was about.

114
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:50,720
那你的老师为什么想跟我们谈谈
Then why does your teacher want to have a chat with us?

115
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:52,360
可能她交不到朋友吧
Maybe she has trouble meeting people.

116
00:03:53,571 --> 00:03:55,420
那是... 好大胆
Oh, that is a -- that's bold.

117
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,740
-太年轻了 是不是 -不会
- It's too young, isn't it? - No!

118
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:59,000
妈呀 这些玩意现在还能测谎了
Oh god, these things have lie detectors now.

119
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,317
先生 请给我看看你的袋子
Sir, please give me your bag.

120
00:04:00,317 --> 00:04:02,300
估计是收银员
Oh...we-- well, the cashier probably

121
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:05,860
忘记取下防盗牌了
just forgot to take a security tag off of the --

122
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:07,080
这是从哪儿来的
Where did that come from?

123
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,640
疑似出现488情况
Possible 488.

124
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:10,620
不是啦 我怎么会偷胸罩
No. I wouldn't steal a bra!

125
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:12,480
我又不穿胸罩
I don't wear bras!

126
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:13,460
可能就穿过一次
Oh. Well, maybe once.

127
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,920
我们的朋友胡娇办过"五十岁好累[变装]派对"
Our friend Pepper had a "Turning 50 is a Drag" party.

128
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,393
他办过五次五十岁生日派对了
Yeah, he's had five of those.

129
00:04:17,393 --> 00:04:18,800
-你懂的 -先生 请随我来
- So... - Sir, please come with me.

130
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,080
不 不不不
No... No, no, no, no, no.

131
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:20,920
米奇尔 打电话叫律师
Mitchell, call a lawyer!

132
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:21,880
我就是律师
I'm a lawyer.

133
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,997
可你输过的官司[丢掉的西装]
Yeah, but you've lost more suits

134
00:04:22,997 --> 00:04:24,442
比遭遇龙卷风的西装大卖场还多
than a Men's Wearhouse in a tornado.

135
00:04:24,442 --> 00:04:25,940
愚人节快乐
April Fool's!

136
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:28,840
他们以为你是商店扒手 傻了吧
They thought you were a shoplifter! Burn!

137
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:32,040
在学校和人打架 现在又搞偷窃恶作剧
A fight at school, and now a shoplifting prank?

138
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,200
如果你这是叛逆期
If you wanted to rebel,

139
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:35,220
为什么不能染一缕粉头发
why don't you just put a pink streak in your hair?

140
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:36,518
我说过了我不想染
I told you, I don't want one.

141
00:04:36,518 --> 00:04:37,820
可你会看起来很可爱的
But you would look so cute.

142
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:39,260
好吧 无论你这是什么阶段
Okay, well, whatever this phase is,

143
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,920
-我可不喜欢 -这都怪我们
- I'm not a fan. - I blame us.

144
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:42,520
-我们太纵容她了 -同意
- We've been far too permissive. - Agreed.

145
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,178
你被禁足一个月 小姑娘
You are grounded for one month, Missy!

146
00:04:45,178 --> 00:04:45,960
太阳马戏团的票已经买了
We got the Cirque du Soleil tickets.

147
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,620
-除了去看太阳马戏团 -和迪斯尼乐园之旅
- Except for Cirque du Soleil! - And the Disneyland trip.

148
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:48,660
和迪斯尼乐园之旅
And for Disneyland!

149
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:51,459
但今晚不准你去克里斯蒂娜的睡衣派对
But you are not going to Christina's slumber party tonight

150
00:04:51,459 --> 00:04:52,957
-无论... -我们今晚订了仙人掌酒店了
- no matter how much -- - We have reservations at Cactus.

151
00:04:52,957 --> 00:04:53,881
好吧 克里斯蒂娜的睡衣派对之后
Okay, Christina's slumber party

152
00:04:53,881 --> 00:04:55,740
近期都不准出去玩
is the last one for a while.

153
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:56,360
没错 没错
Right. That's right.

154
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,600
香薰蜡烛
Scented candles.

155
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,680
愚人的选择
The simpleton's choice.

156
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,254
完美的礼物要有三个元素
The perfect gift has three elements --

157
00:05:09,254 --> 00:05:11,300
不能是你会买给自己的东西
not something you'd buy for yourself,

158
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:12,480
能勾起人的情感回忆
takes you on an emotional journey,

159
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,480
并且勾得很有技巧
that journey is on a ship --

160
00:05:14,987 --> 00:05:16,151
表演技巧
A showmanship.

161
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:20,160
想找到具备三元素的礼物很难
I mean, finding a gift that has all three is challenging,

162
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,440
但重点是 坏点子不是你的敌人
but here's the thing. Bad ideas aren't your enemy.

163
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:24,500
事实上 有时如果你根据坏点子
In fact, sometimes if you free-associate

164
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,520
展开自由联想 就能发现好点子
from the bad ideas, you discover great ones.

165
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:29,140
我们试试看
Let's try it.

166
00:05:29,336 --> 00:05:30,986
先生 您到底想不想买盆栽
Sir, would you like a bonsai tree?

167
00:05:30,986 --> 00:05:32,065
新奇钥匙链
Novelty key chain.

168
00:05:32,065 --> 00:05:33,600
跳进脑海的第一个点子
First thing that popped into the noodle.

169
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,260
糟透了
It's terrible.

170
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,640
我们看看能解锁什么好主意
Let's see what that key unlocks.

171
00:05:35,654 --> 00:05:37,980
新奇钥匙链
Novelty key chain.

172
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:38,836
新奇的锁
Novelty lock.

173
00:05:38,836 --> 00:05:40,560
尼斯湖水怪
Loch Ness Monster.

174
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,313
越野摩托车
Monster bike.

175
00:05:41,313 --> 00:05:43,080
车锁 挂锁
Bike lock. Padlock.

176
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,602
鼠标垫 新奇鼠标垫
Mouse pad. Novelty mouse pad!

177
00:05:44,602 --> 00:05:45,757
新奇钥匙链
Novelty key chain!

178
